; LCNC-SUITE ORIGINAL — not vendored from upstream.
;
; Re-solve the head at the CURRENT table pose, leaving the stored plane alone.
;
; Why this exists. The plane is stored TABLE-relative, so it rides the
; workpiece and can never go stale. The HEAD SOLVE can: orient at A=0, jog the
; table to A=35, and the plane is still on the part while the tool points 35
; deg off its normal. Upstream has no recovery from that short of re-running
; the whole program. This is that recovery, in one action.
;
; It is the same work a first orient does — g53x_core maps the stored plane
; through the live A, solves the rotaries, rewrites the G59 rows and re-enters
; TOOL kinematics. The only difference is that "TWP already active" is the
; normal entry state here rather than an error, which is what M530's Q1 word
; says.
;
; Q1 is an interpreter word and not a HAL demote (M68 E2 Q1 first) on purpose:
; twp-status is an INPUT pin that twp-helper-comp polls to derive
; twp-is-active, so a demote reaches the guard about a millisecond late —
; harmless when an operator types two MDI lines seconds apart, a coin flip
; when a subroutine runs them back to back.
;
; No twp-is-defined guard here: g53x_core already refuses with "No TWP
; defined", and since nothing is demoted on the way in there is no state left
; half-changed when it does.
;
; P word: solution branch, same meaning as G53.1 — 0 = shortest move from the
; current joints, 1 = positive primary rotation only, 2 = negative primary
; only. 0 is the right default for a re-orient: the head is already close and
; wants the small correction, not the program's original branch.

o<twp_reorient>sub

M66 L0 E0                                  ;force sync, stop read ahead
o100 if [EXISTS [#<P>]]
o100 else
    #<P> = 0                               ;default: shortest move
o100 endif
M68 E3 Q0                                  ;identity kinematics for the solve
(WEBUI_KINSTYPE=0)
M66 L0 E0
M530 P#<P> Q1                              ;re-solve, move, re-enter TOOL kins
M66 L0 E0
o<twp_reorient>endsub
m2
